Valve's Steam bridge in the loader: a game's steamclient DLL hands its calls to lsteamclient.

From ValveSoftware/wine, branch proton_11.0 at dc26e61 (LGPL-2.1-or-later), by Valve. Ported to the
CrossOver 26.3.0 tree; the logic is Valve's, unchanged except where noted.

When Wine loads a file named steamclient, steamclient64, gameoverlayrenderer or
gameoverlayrenderer64, it loads lsteamclient.dll beside it and overwrites the start of each exported
function of Valve's file, and its entry point, with a jump to the function of the same name in
lsteamclient. Valve's file stays on disk and in memory. lsteamclient then talks to the native Steam
client (on a Mac, the Steam app's steamclient.dylib). Setting PROTON_DISABLE_LSTEAMCLIENT=1 turns it
off, as in Proton.

- include/winternl.h: the LDR_DONT_CALL_DLLMAIN flag (0x20000000, free in this tree).
- dlls/ntdll/loader.c: use_lsteamclient; import_dll sends steamclient64's and
  gameoverlayrenderer64's tier0_s64/vstdlib_s64 imports to ntdll; MODULE_InitDLL skips modules
  marked LDR_DONT_CALL_DLLMAIN; build_module sets up the jumps. In this tree build_module's flags
  use DONT_RESOLVE_DLL_REFERENCES, where Valve's use LDR_DONT_RESOLVE_REFS.
- dlls/ntdll/unixlib.h, dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c: the steamclient_setup_trampolines Unix call, with
  its wow64 entry for 32-bit games. It sits right after system_time_precise in both call tables,
  before this tree's x86_64-only pe_module_loaded, so 32-bit and 64-bit ntdll agree on its number.

Left out: Valve's WINESTEAMNOEXEC mode (the page fault handler in signal_*.c and its game list). The
jumps are always written. The Unix call logs the number of jumps on the steamclient channel.

lsteamclient itself is not part of this engine: it is built from Proton's source as its own archive,
under Valve's licence. Proton always ships it, so Valve's code does not check for it. Without it, the
loader writes no jumps and a 32-bit steamclient.dll loads as it is; but import_dll still sends the
tier0_s64/vstdlib_s64 imports of steamclient64.dll and gameoverlayrenderer64.dll to ntdll, where each
becomes a stub that fails when called. A program running Valve's own Windows Steam client in this
engine, with no lsteamclient, sets PROTON_DISABLE_LSTEAMCLIENT=1, as Proton's players do.
NotProton (github.com/NotProtonNot/NotProton) showed this bridge working on a Mac with the Mac Steam
app; nothing is copied from it.

Upstream status: Valve's Proton patch; not in WineHQ. Carried here as the one exception in mavrik's
upstream-first rule.

